{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["For <b>Vengeance is Mine, and recompense</b> — to take vengeance for Israel from their hand, and 'and recompense' — to repay them according to their deed, for they denied Me, at the time when their foot slips, when their measure is full, as in the matter of 'for the iniquity of the Amorite is not yet complete' (Genesis 15:16). And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 32:35) that its reason is 'Yea, even the wicked for the day of evil' (Proverbs 16:4), and it is a great secret:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The word שֶׁכִּחֲשׁוּ ('for they denied Me') could also be read as 'in that they lied to Me'; the context of divine retribution for the nations' treatment of Israel supports the rendering adopted."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:30.504355677Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}